INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-swiss-institute-comparative-law', 'organization', 'Swiss Institute of Comparative Law', 'The **Swiss Institute of Comparative Law (Institut suisse de droit comparé - ISDC)** is an autonomous federal research institution based in Lausanne, Switzerland. Established in 1978, the ISDC serves as the preeminent European authority on comparative and international law, advising governments, courts, and international organizations.

### The Council of Europe Circumcision Study
In 2013, the ISDC was commissioned by the Council of Europe to produce the definitive comparative international legal study on the non-therapeutic circumcision of male minors across European and global jurisdictions. The resulting report provided an exhaustive, objective analysis of criminal assault statutes, parental proxy consent limitations, religious freedom protections, and children''s human rights treaties.

### Biolegal Conclusions
The ISDC''s analysis established that in nearly all European legal traditions, the physical integrity of the child is a primary legal right, and that non-therapeutic irreversible surgical procedures performed without the child''s consent sit in deep tension with criminal battery and bodily integrity codes. The study was heavily cited during the drafting of PACE Resolution 1952.

The ISDC remains an authoritative international reference point for comparative legal jurisprudence on bodily autonomy.', 'Preeminent European legal research center that authored the definitive international comparative study on male circumcision for the Council of Europe.', 'notable', 0, 4, 'B+', 'Recognized with a B+ grade for authoring the landmark comparative legal survey establishing that infant circumcision breaches basic child bodily integrity doctrines.', '1978 – Present', 'Swiss Federal Department of Justice, Council of Europe Legal Consultant', 'Comparative Law, International Human Rights, Children''s Rights Jurisprudence, Council of Europe Legal Analysis', 'Authored Comprehensive Comparative Legal Report on Minor Circumcision (2013), Key evidentiary input for PACE Resolution 1952')
