INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-buff', 'organization', 'Brothers United for Future Foreskins (BUFF)', '**Brothers United for Future Foreskins (BUFF)** was one of the earliest pioneering grassroots mutual aid and advocacy organizations founded in the 1980s by circumcised men seeking to reclaim their bodies through non-surgical foreskin restoration.

### Grassroots Origins of Foreskin Restoration
Before the internet and commercial restoration devices, men suffering from physical and emotional circumcision trauma operated in deep isolation. BUFF emerged as an underground network of mutual support, publishing typewritten newsletters, sharing mechanical tissue-expansion experiments (utilizing tape, weights, and manual traction), and offering fraternal validation for men navigating disenfranchised grief.

### Laying the Foundation for NORM
BUFF''s pioneering work proved that mechanical tissue expansion was biologically viable, demonstrating that cellular mitosis could regenerate mucosal and cutaneous shaft tissue. The community and techniques cultivated within BUFF directly inspired the 1989 founding of the **National Organization of Restoring Men (NORM)** by Tim Hammond, Wayne Griffiths, and their peers.

BUFF holds an honored place in intactivist history as the courageous pioneer that transformed foreskin restoration from a private fantasy into an organized, scientifically grounded international healing movement.', 'Pioneering 1980s grassroots foreskin restoration and fraternal mutual aid network that helped catalyze the modern bodily reclamation movement.', 'champion', 0, 5, 'A', 'Awarded an A grade for pioneering the grassroots science and peer brotherhood of foreskin restoration, paving the way for NORM and modern intactivism.', '1984 – 1992', 'NORM Predecessor, Early Restoration Movement', 'Foreskin Restoration, Mechanical Tissue Expansion, Grassroots Mutual Aid, Trauma Processing', 'Published early restoration newsletters, Established first peer support groups for restoring men, Directly catalyzed the founding of NORM')
