INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-pollock-clinics', 'organization', 'Pollock Clinics', 'The **Pollock Clinics** is a high-volume private surgical enterprise headquartered in Vancouver, British Columbia, operating multiple franchised circumcision facilities across Canada and the United States. Founded by Dr. Neil Pollock, the clinic specializes in infant, child, and adult circumcision, promoting a proprietary ''Pollock Technique'' utilizing the Mogen clamp combined with topical and injectable local anesthesia.

### Commercialization and Assembly-Line Marketing
Pollock Clinics exemplifies the aggressive commercialization of elective non-therapeutic pediatric surgery in North America. The clinic markets infant circumcision directly to expectant parents through consumer-focused digital advertising, emphasizing convenience, rapid 30-second procedural speed, and cosmetic standardization. The enterprise actively exports its technique globally, training physicians across North America and participating in international medical export initiatives.

### Clinical and Ethical Critiques
Intactivist organizations, pediatric bioethicists, and surgical critics have scrutinized Pollock Clinics for commodifying the amputation of healthy infant tissue for private profit. Critics note that while Dr. Pollock emphasizes pain management, his business model relies on maintaining cultural demand for elective surgery, downplaying anatomical loss (including the ridged band and frenulum), and minimizing secondary complications like meatal stenosis.

Pollock Clinics stands as a primary case study in how private fee-for-service clinics sustain circumcision rates even as public hospital systems phase out the procedure.', 'High-volume Canadian private circumcision clinic chain exemplifying the commercialized commodification of elective infant surgery.', 'critic', 0, 1, 'F', 'Assigned an F grade for operating high-throughput commercial circumcision factories that prioritize private surgical profit over infant bodily integrity.', '1995 – Present', 'Private Canadian Surgical Sector, Mogen Clamp Industry', 'Commercial Circumcision, Mogen Clamp Technique, Pediatric Cosmetic Surgery, Private Health Marketing', 'Performed over 60,000 infant procedures, Expansion into North American franchise training network')
