INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-pace', 'organization', 'Parliamentary Assembly of the Council of Europe (PACE)', 'The **Parliamentary Assembly of the Council of Europe (PACE)** is the parliamentary body of the Council of Europe, an international human rights organization comprising 46 member states. On October 1, 2013, PACE made international legal history by adopting **Resolution 1952 (2013)**, titled *Children''s Right to Physical Integrity*.

### Landmark Resolution 1952 (2013)
Rapporteured by German parliamentarian Marlene Rupprecht, Resolution 1952 explicitly addressed non-medically justified interventions on children before they are old enough to be consulted. The resolution categorized routine infant male circumcision alongside Female Genital Mutilation (FGM), unnecessary surgical procedures on intersex children, and corporal punishment, defining them as serious violations of children''s rights to bodily integrity under international human rights law.

### Core Directives for Member States
PACE called upon all 46 European member states to:
1. Clearly define the medical and public health conditions under which genital interventions are legally permissible.
2. Initiate public awareness campaigns informing parents of the surgical risks and lack of medical necessity for non-therapeutic circumcision.
3. Adopt legal provisions ensuring that certain operations are not carried out before a child is old enough to participate in the decision.

Resolution 1952 remains the most authoritative multilateral international declaration affirming that infant male circumcision violates universal bodily autonomy rights.', 'Parliamentary body of the Council of Europe that adopted landmark Resolution 1952 (2013) affirming children''s right to physical integrity against non-therapeutic cutting.', 'champion', 1, 5, 'A+', 'Awarded an A+ grade for passing landmark Resolution 1952, the defining international multilateral consensus affirming that infant circumcision violates child bodily integrity.', '1949 – Present', 'Council of Europe, European Court of Human Rights, UN Committee on the Rights of the Child', 'International Human Rights, Physical Integrity of Children, Resolution 1952, Bioethics, Child Protection Treaties', 'Adoption of Resolution 1952 on Children''s Right to Physical Integrity (2013), Recommendation 2023 on Intersex Autonomy')
