INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-ronald-l-poland', 'person', 'Ronald L. Poland, M.D.', '**Ronald L. Poland, M.D.** is an American pediatrician, neonatologist, and academic who served on the American Academy of Pediatrics (AAP) 1989 Task Force on Circumcision. Serving alongside task force chairman Edgar J. Schoen and clinical proponent Thomas E. Wiswell, Poland was instrumental in crafting the policy statement that reversed the AAP''s previous 1975 opposition to routine circumcision.

### The 1989 AAP Policy Reversal
In 1990, Dr. Poland published ''The Question of Routine Neonatal Circumcision'' in the *New England Journal of Medicine*, where he synthesized Wiswell''s controversial research linking the intact foreskin to infant urinary tract infections (UTIs). Poland argued that while circumcision was not absolute, emerging data indicated potential medical benefits that justified parental election of the procedure.

### Academic Defense of Routine Surgery
Throughout the 1990s, Poland defended the AAP''s evolving position against fierce criticism from intactivist organizations, European pediatric societies, and dissenting American bioethicists. Critics pointed out that treating 100 to 200 infants with surgical amputation to theoretically prevent a single easily treatable UTI failed basic risk-benefit bioethics.

Poland remains a central historical figure in the medical establishment''s justification of routine infant circumcision in late-20th-century America.', 'American pediatrician and 1989 AAP Task Force member whose NEJM commentary helped reverse the Academy''s historical opposition to routine circumcision.', 'critic', 0, 1, 'D-', 'Assigned a D- grade for co-authoring the 1989 AAP policy reversal that institutionalized disputed UTI claims and prolonged infant circumcision in America.', '1975 – 2010', 'American Academy of Pediatrics (AAP), Children''s Hospital of Michigan, Penn State Health', 'Neonatology, Pediatric Policy, Urinary Tract Infections, Circumcision Advocacy', 'Co-author of 1989 AAP Task Force Report, Author of 1990 NEJM Circumcision Commentary')
