INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-gerard-zwang', 'person', 'Gérard Zwang, M.D.', '**Gérard Zwang, M.D.** is a prominent French urological surgeon, clinical sexologist, and author who was among the earliest and most vocal European surgeons to scientifically condemn routine male circumcision as a sexual and anatomical mutilation. Author of over fifty books on human sexuality and urology, including *Abrégé de sexologie* (1972) and *La statuaire érotique* (1983), Dr. Zwang is considered a foundational figure in French medical sexology.

### The Erotic Architecture of the Prepuce
Dr. Zwang rejected the Anglo-American framing of the foreskin as redundant or pathogenic skin. Utilizing surgical and histological evidence, he demonstrated that the prepuce is a primary erogenous organ equipped with specialized mechanoreceptors, specialized dartos muscle fibers, and a vascular network engineered specifically to facilitate frictionless sexual intercourse and preserve the sensitivity of the glans.

### Critique of the ''Anglo-Saxon Obsession''
Throughout his career, Dr. Zwang characterized routine infant circumcision in the United States as an irrational ''cultural neurosis'' masquerading as science, rooted in Victorian anti-masturbatory hysteria. He consistently affirmed that excising the foreskin amounts to a permanent reduction in sexual capacity, sensory pleasure, and bodily wholeness.

His clinical treatises provided European urologists and intactivists with rigorous anatomical arguments that helped shield continental Europe from adopting routine neonatal circumcision.', 'Pioneering French urologist and sexologist whose anatomical treatises established the irreplaceable erotic and biomechanical functions of the human foreskin.', 'champion', 1, 5, 'A+', 'Awarded an A+ grade for decades of pioneering urological scholarship demonstrating that the foreskin is an essential, irreplaceable sensory organ.', '1965 – 2015', 'French Urological Community, French Society of Clinical Sexology', 'Urological Surgery, Preputial Erotic Anatomy, Clinical Sexology, Anti-Circumcision Treatise', 'Publication of ''Abrégé de sexologie'' (1972), Seminal treatises on prepuce biomechanics, International Lectures on Genital Preservation')
