INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-jutta-reisinger', 'person', 'Dr. Jutta Reisinger', '**Dr. Jutta Reisinger** is an Austrian physician and clinical investigator recognized for her critical field research into Voluntary Medical Male Circumcision (VMMC) campaigns in sub-Saharan Africa. Her observations and whistleblowing reports were prominently featured in the 2025 Deutsche Welle (DW) documentary *Cut, Uncut*.

### Exposing WHO Field Conditions in Kenya
Having observed clinical operations in Kenya funded by international health initiatives, Dr. Reisinger documented severe discrepancies between official World Health Organization protocols and on-the-ground reality. She reported on makeshift rural clinics performing high-speed surgical procedures under non-sterile conditions, inadequate postoperative follow-up, and significant rates of hemorrhage, infection, and irreversible penile disfigurement.

### The Ethics of Mass Surgical Interventions
Dr. Reisinger has been a leading European clinical voice questioning the epidemiological foundations of VMMC mass campaigns. She has argued that relying on surgical amputation of healthy genital tissue as a primary prophylactic against HIV in developing nations is bioethically flawed, cost-ineffective compared to barrier contraception, and perpetuates Western medical paternalism.

Her courage in speaking out against institutional orthodoxy has provided essential empirical backing for European bioethicists and international bodily autonomy advocates.', 'Austrian physician whose field observations in East Africa exposed clinical malpractice and ethical failures in international VMMC campaigns.', 'champion', 0, 5, 'A', 'Awarded an A grade for clinical integrity in documenting and exposing the severe surgical hazards and coercive practices of mass African circumcision campaigns.', '2015 – Present', 'European Medical Community, Deutsche Welle Whistleblower', 'VMMC Field Conditions, Global Public Health Ethics, Surgical Complications, African Health Policy', 'Feature testimony in DW Documentary ''Cut, Uncut'' (2025), Field Reports on Kenyan Circumcision Clinics')
