INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-silja-dogg-gunnarsdottir', 'person', 'Silja Dögg Gunnarsdóttir', '**Silja Dögg Gunnarsdóttir** is an Icelandic politician who served as a Member of the Althing (Icelandic Parliament) representing the Progressive Party from 2013 to 2021. In February 2018, Gunnarsdóttir introduced a historic legislative bill that made Iceland the first European country to formally debate a statutory prohibition on non-therapeutic male circumcision of minors.

### The 2018 Icelandic Legislative Bill
Gunnarsdóttir''s bill proposed amending the Icelandic Penal Code to establish a penalty of up to six years'' imprisonment for performing non-therapeutic circumcision on a boy unable to give informed consent. She framed the legislation strictly through a child-rights and bodily integrity lens, citing Article 24(3) of the United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child, which obligates states to abolish traditional practices prejudicial to the health of children.

### International Discourse and Medical Support
The bill garnered overwhelming public support in Iceland and strong formal endorsements from the Icelandic Medical Association, the Icelandic Association of Nurses, and Nordic pediatric societies. While facing severe diplomatic pushback and international religious pressure that ultimately stalled parliamentary passage, Gunnarsdóttir''s initiative fundamentally elevated the issue of boy genital autonomy onto the international diplomatic and legislative stage.

Her courage in sponsoring the bill demonstrated the viability of legislative reform within modern democratic legal systems committed to universal child protection.', 'Icelandic parliamentarian who introduced Europe''s first legislative bill to prohibit non-therapeutic infant male circumcision on child rights grounds.', 'champion', 1, 5, 'A+', 'Awarded an A+ grade for courageous parliamentary leadership in introducing the first European statutory ban on non-therapeutic infant circumcision.', '2013 – 2021', 'Althing (Parliament of Iceland), Progressive Party, Nordic Council', 'Legislative Reform, Child Rights, UNCRC Article 24(3), Bodily Integrity, European Bioethics', 'Introduction of Parliamentary Bill 114 (2018), Endorsement by Icelandic Medical Association, Historic European Parliamentary Debate')
