INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-eric-clopper', 'person', 'Eric Clopper, Esq.', '**Eric Clopper, Esq.** is an American attorney, author, and civil rights advocate who has brought prominent legal, cultural, and theatrical challenges against routine infant male circumcision in the United States. A graduate of Harvard University, Clopper gained international attention in 2018 with his multimedia theatrical production and legal presentation *Sex and Circumcision: An American Love Story*, staged at Harvard''s Sanders Theatre.

### Constitutional & Equal Protection Jurisprudence
Clopper''s legal scholarship centers on the application of the Fourteenth Amendment''s Equal Protection Clause and substantive due process to bodily integrity. He argues that statutory frameworks prohibiting Female Genital Mutilation (FGM) while leaving male infants without legal protection from non-therapeutic genital alteration constitute unconstitutional sex-based discrimination under heightened judicial scrutiny.

### Impact Litigation: Hadachek and Huff
Clopper has served as lead counsel and strategic legal advisor in pioneering federal constitutional challenges, including *Hadachek v. State of Oregon* (filed in U.S. District Court in March 2025) and *Huff v. State of Colorado*. These lawsuits challenge state statutes that exempt non-therapeutic male circumcision from child abuse, assault, and mutilation laws, arguing that children possess a fundamental, inalienable right to an intact body regardless of sex.

### Intact Global & Public Education
Through his organization **Intact Global**, Clopper has convened international conferences, produced extensive educational lectures, and provided media commentary deconstructing the historical, psychological, and financial mechanisms that perpetuate infant circumcision in American hospitals.', 'Civil rights attorney, creator of ''Sex and Circumcision: An American Love Story'', and lead litigator advancing 14th Amendment equal protection for children.', 'champion', 1, 5, 'A+', 'Awarded an A+ grade for pioneering innovative constitutional impact litigation establishing that infant male circumcision violates the Equal Protection Clause.', '2018 – Present', 'Intact Global (Founder), Harvard University, GALDEF, Hadachek v. Oregon Legal Team', 'Constitutional Law, 14th Amendment Equal Protection, Sex Discrimination, Child Bodily Integrity, Impact Litigation', 'Sanders Theatre Presentation (2018), Hadachek v. Oregon Filing (2025), Huff v. Colorado Co-Counsel, Intact Global Conferences')
