INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-christopher-cold', 'person', 'Christopher J. Cold, M.D.', '**Christopher J. Cold, M.D.** is an American clinical pathologist, anatomist, and scholarly pioneer in preputial functional morphology. Serving as a pathologist at the Marshfield Clinic and clinical professor at the University of Wisconsin Medical School, Dr. Cold has dedicated decades to illuminating the specialized micro-anatomy and neuro-vascular complexity of the foreskin.

### The Landmark 1999 Monograph: ''The Prepuce''
In 1999, Dr. Cold co-authored the definitive anatomical review *The prepuce* with Dr. John R. Taylor, published in the *British Journal of Urology International*. The monograph synthesized decades of histological, immunological, and mechanical research, demonstrating that the prepuce is not inert ''skin'' but an elaborate mucocutaneous specialized organ with five primary functions:
1. Mechanical protection and lubrication of the glans penis
2. Immunological defense via Langerhans cells and secretory immunoglobulins
3. Specialized sensory innervation featuring Meissner''s corpuscles, Vater-Pacini corpuscles, and genital end-bulbs
4. Dynamic gliding action reducing shear forces and friction during intercourse
5. Erogenous stimulation via the ridged band and ventral frenulum

Dr. Cold''s meticulous microphotographs and histological preparations remain standard reference material across global bioethics and medical education.', 'Pathologist and co-author of the landmark 1999 BJU International anatomical treatise detailing the prepuce''s specialized immunological, mechanical, and erogenous architecture.', 'champion', 1, 5, 'A+', 'Awarded an A+ grade for decades of anatomical research detailing the histological and physiological indispensability of the human prepuce.', '1990 – Present', 'Marshfield Clinic, University of Wisconsin Medical School, BJU International', 'Surgical Pathology, Preputial Micro-Anatomy, Histology, Erogenous Receptors, Mechanical Gliding Action', 'Co-author of ''The Prepuce'' (BJU International 1999), Marshfield Clinic Histological Series, Medical Expert in Genital Autonomy Symposia')
