INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-tone-pettit', 'person', 'Tone Pettit', '**Tone Pettit** is an independent Seattle-based researcher, data scientist, writer, and the creator of **The Accidental Intactivist** and the **CircumSurvey** research platform.

Born in the 1970s and raised intact as a statistical outlier in the United States—where routine infant circumcision (RIC) was the unquestioned 90% norm—Tone grew up outside the cultural spell, looking at the practice through the lens of an "accidental anthropologist" with the persistent question: *"Why isn''t this weird to more of us?"*

### Empirical Research & Data Science
Rather than relying on ideological rhetoric, Tone spearheaded the creation of CircumSurvey to capture rigorous empirical microdata directly from thousands of men worldwide. His work maps the physical, sexual, and psychological outcomes of circumcision, including the foundational analysis of the "pleasure gap," sexual satisfaction disparities, erectile mechanics, and the reasons men pursue foreskin restoration.

### The Manifesto & Legal Analysis
Tone is the author of *The Accidental Intactivist''s Guide: A Critical Analysis of Routine Infant Circumcision* (published across [Substack](https://theaccidentalintactivist.substack.com), [Medium](https://medium.com/@theaccidentalintactivist), and academic editions), duplicating core analytical tables and daylighting the medical and cultural retcons that sustain RIC. In 2026, he conducted frontline field analysis of *Hadachek v. Oregon*, exposing the State''s attempts to legally categorize child bodily autonomy as a "female privilege."

### Guiding Philosophy
Tone''s work champions the principle of *"Not about us without us"* and the stoic realization that historical grievances cannot be rewritten, but future culture can be transformed by intentional, confident advocacy grounded in unassailable empirical truth.', 'Seattle-based data scientist, lead researcher of CircumSurvey, author of The Accidental Intactivist''s Guide, and creator of the genital autonomy research platform.', 'champion', 1, 5, 'A+', 'Awarded an A+ grade as the lead researcher, creator of CircumSurvey, and author of The Accidental Intactivist''s Guide for pioneering data-driven bodily autonomy investigation and daylighting the cultural pleasure gap.', '2012 – Present', 'CircumSurvey (Lead Researcher & Creator), The Accidental Intactivist, r/FriendsoftheFrenulum', 'Empirical Survey Data, Cultural Cognitive Dissonance, Pleasure Gap Analysis, Bodily Autonomy, Bioethics', 'Launch of CircumSurvey Platform, The Accidental Intactivist Manifesto, 6 Core Analytical Pleasure Gap Tables, Awakenings Dataset Modernization, Hadachek Field Note Analysis (2026)')
