INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-4d4cb5c1', 'organization', 'American Academy of Pediatrics (AAP)', 'The American Academy of Pediatrics (AAP) is a primary professional association of pediatricians in the United States, established in 1930 and dedicated to the health, safety, and well-being of infants, children, adolescents, and young adults. As a major standard-setting body in American clinical practice, the AAP issues policy statements, clinical guidance, and educational materials that exert a powerful influence on neonatal and pediatric care standards nationally and internationally. 

Within the archival record of the genital autonomy and intactivism movement, the AAP occupies a central and contested position, primarily functioning as an institutional critic of total prohibitions on non-therapeutic infant penile cutting, while serving as a frequent target of human rights critique. The academy''s historical policy statements and related pediatric publications—including content scrutinized in formal evaluations such as the *JAMA Pediatrics Circumcision Patient Page Correction Analysis and Impact Report*—are extensively examined for their clinical, methodological, and ethical rationales regarding infant circumcision. International bioethical authorities, such as those responsible for *Opinion no. 70 of 8 May 2017 on the ethical aspects of nonmedical circumcision*, have routinely placed the AAP''s positions in sharp contrast with human rights principles and European medical consensus. Furthermore, foundational movement texts, personal accounts, and empirical investigations—including *AWAKENINGS: A Preliminary Poll of Circumcised Men Revealing the Long-Term Harm and Healing the Wounds of Infant Circumcision*, *The Accidental Intactivist Manifesto*, and scientific studies examining the sexual correlates of neonatal circumcision in adult men—frequently challenge the AAP’s institutional narrative by confronting its permissive guidelines with the lived experiences, psychosexual outcomes, and bodily integrity rights of affected individuals.', 'The primary American pediatric association whose influential policy statements have historically affirmed the health benefits of routine infant male circumcision.', 'critic', 1, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
