INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-cd74c95a', 'organization', 'National Organization to Halt the Abuse and Routine Mutilation of Males (NOHARMM)', 'The **National Organization to Halt the Abuse and Routine Mutilation of Males (NOHARMM)** is an advocacy organization and pioneering champion within the international movement for genital autonomy. Established to oppose non-therapeutic infant circumcision, the organization has consistently operated as a dedicated voice for men impacted by early genital cutting, framing the defense of bodily integrity as a fundamental human rights issue. 

NOHARMM has played an integral role in documenting and amplifying the physical and psychological consequences of routine neonatal cutting. Its seminal efforts include supporting preliminary research and polling—such as the survey work represented in *AWAKENINGS: A Preliminary Poll of Circumcised Men Revealing the Long-Term Harm and Healing the Wounds of Infant Circumcision*—which examined long-term trauma, psychological healing, and the grief experienced by affected men. Furthermore, NOHARMM’s work serves as a foundational reference in historical and cultural analyses of medicalized circumcision in North America, particularly concerning shifting perceptions of neonatal pain and masculinity throughout the latter half of the twentieth century.

Beyond grass-roots support and psychological documentation, NOHARMM’s contributions intersect with broader clinical, legal, and human rights scholarship. The organization is frequently cited in academic literature evaluating the adverse outcomes of cutting on adult male sexual function, as well as comparative legal and cross-cultural analyses addressing the ritual legitimization of both male and female genital alteration under theological frameworks. Through this multifaceted engagement, NOHARMM has sustained a critical role as an early institutional champion for comprehensive genital autonomy and bodily rights.', 'Pioneering advocacy organization founded in 1992 to educate the public on the harms of male circumcision and advance genital autonomy.', 'champion', 1, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
