INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-30c26dc6', 'organization', 'UNCIRC', '**UNCIRC** (the Uncircumcising Information and Resource Center) is an early, pioneering organization and foundational champion within the global movement for genital autonomy. Established to address the psychological and physical aftermath of non-therapeutic neonatal circumcision, UNCIRC emerged as one of the first organized clearinghouses dedicated to the support of circumcised men, the promotion of non-surgical foreskin restoration, and the defense of bodily integrity. Operating at the intersection of men’s health, education, and human rights, the organization provided crucial guidance during the formative years of contemporary intactivism, offering practical alternatives and emotional validation to individuals seeking to reclaim their anatomical wholeness.

Throughout historical intactivist literature, UNCIRC is widely recognized for its multi-faceted contributions to advocacy, education, and peer support. The organization has served as a central reference point in critical inquiries into the long-term harm of infant circumcision, contributing to early surveys and documentations of men’s trauma and healing pathways, such as the landmark study *AWAKENINGS*. Beyond its dedicated focus on foreskin restoration techniques—articulating both the biological value of the prepuce and practical methods for tissue expansion—UNCIRC''s educational outreach extended to the preservation of intact anatomy. Its literature consistently advocated for the proper care of the intact penis, warning against harmful practices like forced prepuce retraction in infancy and challenging clinical overdiagnosis. As a result, UNCIRC remains permanently codified across movement bibliographies, resource directories, and educational treatises as an indispensable vanguard in the restoration of men''s voices and bodily autonomy.', 'An advocacy and resource organization dedicated to promoting genital autonomy, foreskin restoration awareness, and education opposing non-consensual circumcision.', 'champion', 0, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET
