INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-f73385df', 'person', 'Ronald Goldman', 'Ronald Goldman is a pioneering researcher, psychologist, and prominent champion within the intactivist movement for genital autonomy. His scholarly and clinical contributions have served as a critical pillar in understanding non-therapeutic infant circumcision through the lens of human rights, psychological trauma, and somatic memory. Goldman''s work shifted the discourse from purely anatomical considerations to the profound mental, developmental, and emotional effects of early bodily alteration.

Throughout the literature of the genital autonomy movement, Goldman is widely cited for his foundational research into the acute pain, enduring psychological trauma, and complex psychosexual sequelae associated with male circumcision. His contributions explore the institutional and cultural resistance to acknowledging these harms, aligning with broader analyses that position non-consensual genital modifications within systems of gender power politics. Goldman’s work also intersects critically with legal and ethical inquiries that analyze the disparate treatment of male and female genital alteration under international human rights frameworks, illustrating where entrenched cultural practices collide with legal standards of bodily integrity.

As a foundational figure examined in both historical overviews of the modern movement''s origins and contemporary manifestos challenging societal silence, Goldman’s advocacy has shaped the trajectory of intactivism. By documenting the hidden psychological costs of neonatal intervention, his body of work continues to validate the lived experiences of affected individuals and remains instrumental in advancing the recognition of full genital autonomy for all children.', 'Psychologist, executive director of the Circumcision Resource Center, and author of ''Circumcision: The Hidden Trauma''.', 'champion', 1, 5, 'A+', 'Awarded an A+ grade for pioneering clinical psychology research examining PTSD, psychological defense mechanisms, and intimacy trauma in circumcised men.', '', '', '', '')
