INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-983a1457', 'organization', 'Foregen', '**Foregen** is an organization and leading champion within the global intactivist and genital autonomy movements, recognized for advancing regenerative medicine solutions for circumcised men. Operating at the intersection of bioethics, human rights, and biotechnology, the organization seeks to establish viable clinical pathways to biologically regenerate the human prepuce, offering a restorative therapeutic alternative to individuals subjected to non-consensual infant genital cutting.

Within the archival literature of the genital integrity movement, Foregen represents an evolution in restorative advocacy, extending beyond conventional mechanical foreskin restoration into the realm of advanced cellular therapies. Its mission and scientific framework are documented across foundational activist texts, including *The Accidental Intactivist Manifesto: Exposing the Monster We Agree Not to See*, as well as in comprehensive studies focusing on foreskin restorers. These records capture how Foregen’s regenerative goals intersect with the motivations, challenges, and clinical experiences of men consulting medical and mental health professionals to address the physical, sensory, and psychological fallout of circumcision.

Foregen’s research initiatives have also brought critical attention to the sheer demographic scale and economic scope of the restoration community. Movement survey data associated with Foregen highlights an addressable regenerative market estimated at over 200 billion dollars, reflecting an affected cohort of tens of millions of men seeking bodily restitution. Through its pursuit of bio-restoration and its integration into the wider discourse on genital autonomy, Foregen serves as a prominent force dedicated to remedying bodily harm and vindicating the right to physical integrity.', 'A non-profit biotechnology organization dedicated to regenerating foreskin tissue through regenerative medicine for circumcised men.', 'champion', 1, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
