INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-1d74fe87', 'person', 'Georganne Chapin', '**Georganne Chapin** is an advocate and champion within the intactivism and genital autonomy movement, known for her interdisciplinary work at the intersection of bioethics, healthcare policy, and human rights. Her advocacy focuses on defending the fundamental right of all children to bodily integrity and challenging institutional medical practices that condone or perform non-therapeutic genital cutting on minors. 

Chapin’s contributions prominently feature in critical analyses of medical policy and institutional ethics. She has played a notable role in public health dialogues scrutinizing pediatric guidelines, including debates surrounding the American Academy of Pediatrics (AAP) and the significant pushback that led to the retraction of its controversial policy statement regarding a "ritual nick" as an alternative form of female genital alteration. Beyond institutional critiques, Chapin’s work and perspective are integrated into broader academic and psychological frameworks, such as the conceptualization of child genital cutting as an Adverse Childhood Experience (ACE) and sociological research exploring embodiment, bodily integrity, and child-rearing norms within American pro-breastfeeding and anti-circumcision movements.

Through critical evaluations of medical commodification—such as her engagement with the issues highlighted in *Don’t Ask, Don’t Sell*—Chapin has addressed the ethical implications and financial incentives underpinning neonatal circumcision and tissue harvesting. As a steadfast champion of bodily autonomy, her work continues to inform the global movement to establish universal legal and cultural protections against involuntary genital cutting.', 'Founder and Executive Director of Intact America and prominent advocate for children''s genital integrity and bioethics.', 'champion', 0, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
