INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-d857a8ff', 'person', 'Morten Frisch', '**Morten Frisch** is a Danish physician, epidemiologist, and scholarly champion within the international movement for genital autonomy. Recognized for his rigorous epidemiological research and dedication to bioethics, Frisch has served as a central scientific voice examining the medical, cultural, and human rights dimensions of non-therapeutic male circumcision, consistently advocating for evidence-based medicine and the bodily integrity of non-consenting minors.

Within the literature of genital autonomy, Frisch is internationally prominent for challenging medical policy statements that reflect regional and cultural biases rather than neutral scientific consensus. He notably spearheaded the high-profile European medical critique *Cultural Bias in the AAP’s 2012 Technical Report and Policy Statement on Male Circumcision*, which engaged the American Academy of Pediatrics Task Force in a consequential global dialogue concerning ethical standards and pediatric welfare. His academic interventions further include formal evaluations challenging draft circumcision recommendations from the U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) on medical, procedural, and legal grounds. 

In addition to policy analysis, Frisch has contributed substantially to the scientific debate surrounding the long-term anatomical and physiological consequences of male circumcision. His critical commentaries—particularly in response to disputed studies regarding sexual sensation, function, and satisfaction—have provided vital counterarguments to assertions minimizing the procedure''s negative effects. Through these interdisciplinary contributions, as well as analyses interrogating the broader legitimacy and ethical framing of the practice, Frisch remains an indispensable scholar in the defense of children''s rights to bodily autonomy.', 'Danish epidemiologist, Statens Serum Institut consultant, and lead author of the 38-expert international rebuttal to the AAP 2012 policy in Pediatrics.', 'champion', 1, 5, 'A+', 'Awarded an A+ grade for organizing the 38-expert European pediatric coalition in Pediatrics (2013) that daylighted the cultural bias and statistical flaws of the AAP.', '', '', '', '')
