INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-0bf5f0fd', 'person', 'Andrew L. Freedman', '**Andrew L. Freedman, M.D.**, is an American pediatric urologist whose work has placed him at the center of institutional and ethical debates surrounding non-therapeutic neonatal male circumcision. Most notably recognized for his involvement with the American Academy of Pediatrics (AAP) Task Force on Circumcision, Freedman has served as a prominent institutional voice in articulating the clinical positions of the American pediatric establishment on the procedure.

Within the literature of the genital autonomy and intactivism movement, Freedman’s work and policy contributions frequently serve as key subjects of critical analysis. Scholars and advocates for bodily integrity have extensively engaged with his positions, examining the evidentiary and ethical frameworks underpinning institutional guidelines. His arguments are closely scrutinized in key bioethical and medical critiques, such as *The AAP report on circumcision: Bad science + bad ethics = bad medicine* and *Cultural Bias in American Medicine: The Case of Infant Male Circumcision*, where critics challenge the medical validity and cultural assumptions embedded in professional recommendations.

Freedman''s role in the circumcision debate also intersects with broader human rights and legal inquiries regarding consent and harm. His positions are addressed in foundational discussions concerning decision-making authority—such as *Male circumcision: Who should decide?*—as well as comprehensive critiques exploring long-term physical and experiential impacts, including *Circumcision, Sexual Experience, and Harm* and *Is Circumcision a Fraud?*. Across the movement''s archive, Freedman is positioned as an influential clinical proponent whose published defenses of circumcision remain central touchstones for ongoing debates on children''s rights and genital autonomy.', 'Pediatric urologist and co-chair of the 2012 AAP Task Force on Circumcision', 'critic', 1, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
