INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-cd0fc853', 'person', 'Angela Merkel', '**Angela Merkel** (born July 17, 1954) is a German politician who served as the Chancellor of Germany from 2005 to 2021. Within the scholarly archive of the genital autonomy and intactivism movement, Merkel is primarily documented as a prominent political critic of legal efforts to prohibit or restrict non-therapeutic infant male circumcision. Her administration played a decisive role in shaping contemporary European policy and jurisprudence on children''s bodily integrity following landmark judicial challenges in Germany.

Merkel''s political interventions are extensively analyzed in comparative political and legal literature addressing circumcision bans across Western Europe. Following the 2012 Cologne regional court ruling that classified non-therapeutic male circumcision as bodily harm, Merkel strongly opposed prohibitionist stances, emphasizing national identity, freedom of religion, and minority inclusion in Germany. Under her leadership, the German government swiftly codified explicit statutory protections permitting parental authorization of male circumcision, a development frequently examined in human rights literature regarding the regulation of childhood genital modifications. Within intactivist discourse, her legacy serves as a central case study in the tensions between international children''s rights frameworks, state secularity, and the political accommodation of cultural and religious traditions.', 'Former Chancellor of Germany who spearheaded federal legislation to legalise non-therapeutic male circumcision following a landmark 2012 court ruling.', 'critic', 1, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
