INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-bb85f93a', 'person', 'Lauren M. Sardi', '**Lauren M. Sardi** is a notable academic researcher and scholar whose empirical work has contributed significantly to the sociological and psychological literature surrounding genital autonomy and the intactivist movement. Sardi’s scholarship focuses on examining the cultural, ideological, and medical dynamics surrounding male circumcision, particularly analyzing the cognitive rationalizations of circumcision status, the lived experiences of affected individuals, and the evolving strategies of anti-circumcision activism.

A central area of Sardi’s contribution lies in the empirical study of foreskin restoration. Through comprehensive investigations—including key research on the motivations, outcomes, and systemic challenges faced by restorers—Sardi has documented the psychological and physical journeys of individuals seeking to reclaim genital integrity, with particular attention to their often fraught encounters with medical and mental health professionals. Complementing this clinical and personal focus, Sardi has also investigated the perceptual frameworks surrounding circumcision, co-authoring research demonstrating how cognitive biases and false beliefs correlate with and predict satisfaction with circumcision status among American men.

Beyond the psychological and anatomical dimensions of genital autonomy, Sardi has critically analyzed intactivism as a broader sociopolitical movement. Her scholarship charts the historical trajectory of anti-circumcision discourse—such as early popular critiques published in men’s magazines—while offering nuanced examinations of modern, digital-era activism. In studies addressing ideology, privilege, and equity across social media platforms, Sardi has evaluated how contemporary activists construct their advocacy, navigate intersectional dynamics, and organize in pursuit of universal bodily integrity.', 'Sociologist and scholar whose research examines the cultural, gendered, and medicalized dimensions of infant circumcision and bodily autonomy.', 'notable', 0, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
