INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-83ad8220', 'person', 'Jeannine Parvati Baker', '**Jeannine Parvati Baker** stands as an influential figure and champion within the movement for genital autonomy and bodily integrity. Across seminal literature and historical records of the intactivist movement, her advocacy linked the protection of natural anatomy and the rights of the newborn to broader ethical and human rights frameworks, challenging normalized medicalized interventions such as infant circumcision.

Baker was a prominent contributor to early international dialogues on genital integrity, appearing as a distinguished presenter at key assemblies including the Second International Symposium on Circumcision as well as subsequent Genital Integrity Conferences. Her participation in these international symposia—preserved across presenter biographies, conference programs, and proceedings associated with human rights honors—underscores her role as a dedicated educator and public advocate. 

In addition to her conference addresses, Baker’s insights are documented in archival movement publications and commentary, including *The Hand That Rocks the Circumstraint Board* and movement editorial records. Through these contributions, Baker critiqued routine clinical practices and urged both parents and healthcare practitioners to respect the fundamental right of infants to an intact body, solidifying her legacy within the intellectual history of genital autonomy.', 'Midwife, author, and natural birth pioneer who advocated for infant bodily integrity and opposed routine infant circumcision.', 'champion', 0, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
