INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-69e4d7ba', 'organization', 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC)', 'The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) is the national public health institute of the United States. Within the broader discourse of genital autonomy and human rights, the agency occupies a significant and frequently contested institutional position. The CDC has actively formulated guidance regarding prophylactic genital cutting, producing formal syntheses of scientific literature to guide healthcare professionals, most notably through its guidance titled *Information for Providers to Share with Male Patients and Parents Regarding Male Circumcision and the Prevention of HIV Infection, Sexually Transmitted Infections, and other Health Outcomes*. In addition to its guidance concerning infant circumcision, the agency has assessed the implementation of adult circumcision to reduce HIV transmission, including examining willingness and uptake among men who have sex with men (MSM) in the United States.

Within the archival literature of intactivism and bioethics, the CDC is prominently engaged not only as an institutional public health body but also as a primary target of criticism by advocates for bodily integrity. Scholars addressing the legal, ethical, and public health dimensions of circumcision regularly scrutinize the CDC’s reliance on data from sub-Saharan African randomized clinical trials, raising substantial methodological, legal, and ethical objections to their application in domestic policy. The agency’s guidelines have prompted rigorous formal evaluations and challenges—such as scholarly debates analyzing formal critiques of the CDC’s male circumcision recommendations. Consequently, the CDC stands within the movement''s records as a key institutional proponent of medicalized circumcision whose policies remain central to ongoing human rights debates concerning state-sponsored health initiatives and individual bodily autonomy.', 'The primary United States public health agency, notable in circumcision discourse for issuing guidelines asserting that the health benefits of male circumcision outweigh the risks.', 'critic', 1, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
