INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-5b6ab355', 'person', 'Allan J. Jacobs', '**Allan J. Jacobs** is a bioethicist and scholar whose work serves as a significant focal point in the academic debates surrounding bodily integrity and child rights. Within the intellectual discourse of the intactivist movement, Jacobs is primarily recognized as a prominent critic of efforts to prohibit or legally restrict non-therapeutic neonatal circumcision. His scholarship—frequently developed in collaboration with Kavita Shah Arora—advocates for the social and legal accommodation of the procedure, emphasizing tolerance for ritual male infant circumcision and advising caution against proposals to criminalize medically unnecessary child genital cutting in Western jurisdictions.

Because of his defense of the practice, Jacobs'' arguments have drawn extensive critical analysis from human rights theorists, bioethicists, and advocates of the genital autonomy movement. His positions, particularly concerning the ethical frameworks balancing parental authority, religious tradition, and children''s rights, have been directly examined and challenged in major scholarly treatises including *In defence of genital autonomy for children*, *Cutting Both Ways: On the Ethical Entanglements of Human Rights, Rites, and Genital Mutilation*, and *The Mysterious Disappearance of the Object of Inquiry: Jacobs and Arora''s Defense of Circumcision*. Within the broader movement for genital autonomy, Jacobs remains a central interlocutor whose defenses of circumcision are frequently analyzed to articulate the human rights principles supporting a child''s right to an intact body.', 'American physician and bioethicist known for his academic defenses of the ethics and permissibility of infant male circumcision.', 'critic', 1, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
