INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-7206e711', 'person', 'Marie Fox', '**Marie Fox** is a distinguished legal scholar, bioethicist, and champion of bodily integrity within the global movement for genital autonomy. Her academic work critically examines the intersections of health law, jurisprudence, and human rights, establishing her as an influential voice challenging the legal and ethical justifications for non-therapeutic male circumcision. Through rigorous scholarship, Fox has consistently argued that non-consensual bodily modifications infringe upon fundamental principles of physical autonomy and children''s rights.

Her contributions have substantially shaped modern intactivist and bioethical discourse. Fox has analyzed the socio-political dimensions of health policy, particularly examining public health mandates such as global circumcision campaigns related to HIV/AIDS and formal risk-benefit evaluations, including critical appraisals of proposed Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) guidelines. Furthermore, Fox has contributed to the integration of gender studies and legal theory into the movement, elucidating how bodily integrity is fundamentally aligned with feminist principles and demonstrating that the defense of the foreskin is an essential feminist issue.

Fox’s scholarly assessments, most notably foundational writings such as *Short Changed? The Law and Ethics of Male Circumcision*, have extended beyond academia into the realm of legal precedent. Her critical analyses of parental proxy consent and state intervention have informed judicial perspectives on the matter, earning citations in high-profile custody and bodily autonomy proceedings such as the landmark legal case *Boldt v. Boldt*. Through her sustained inquiry into law, ethics, and social justice, Fox continues to be an essential intellectual figure in articulating genital autonomy as an inalienable human right.', 'British legal scholar and bioethicist known for her critical legal analysis of non-consensual male infant circumcision and children''s rights to bodily integrity.', 'champion', 0, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
