INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-78cec8f3', 'person', 'Guy Cox', '**Guy Cox** is a scholar and scientific champion within the movement for genital autonomy, whose work bridges anatomical science, evolutionary biology, and the medical ethics surrounding infant and child bodily integrity. His scholarly engagements critically examine the physiological, histological, and functional significance of the human prepuce, providing vital counter-perspectives to non-therapeutic circumcision within peer-reviewed biomedical literature.

Cox’s contributions span key academic dialogues concerning the biological functions and subjective realities of the intact male body. He has explored the functional significance of the human prepuce through an evolutionary lens in *De Virginibus Puerisque: The Function of the Human Foreskin Considered from an Evolutionary Perspective*, as well as its fine-structural anatomy and neurological role in *Histological Correlates of Penile Sexual Sensation: Does Circumcision Make a Difference?*. In addition to histological and functional inquiries, Cox has addressed the broader psychological and personal impact of non-consensual modifications, engaging with the subjective dimensions of foreskin loss. 

Within the broader medical debate, Cox has actively contested institutional and academic rationalizations for infant circumcision. His perspective features prominently in rigorous scientific exchanges, including critical rebuttals such as *Re: The medical evidence on non-therapeutic circumcision of infants and boys—setting the record straight*, as well as direct scholarly responses to polemics framing the practice as a biomedical imperative. Through this sustained body of academic inquiry, Cox remains an influential voice championing evidence-based anatomy, sexual health, and the universal right to bodily integrity.', 'Australian academic and advocate for genital integrity who served as a leading voice against infant circumcision in Australia.', 'champion', 0, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
