INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-800baa2c', 'person', 'George Williams', 'George Williams is a dedicated champion within the movement for genital autonomy, whose sustained engagement contributed to the advocacy and discourse surrounding the protection of children from non-therapeutic circumcision. Emerging into prominence during the vital organizational expansion of the 1990s, Williams was an active voice documented in central movement publications. His efforts were chronicled in the National Organization of Circumcision Information Resource Centers (*NOCIRC Newsletter*, Spring 1994; *NOCIRC Fall 1999 Update*) as well as in grassroots periodicals such as *The Guardian Angell* (January 1995), reflecting his long-standing commitment to advancing public and institutional awareness of bodily integrity as a fundamental human right.

Beyond foundational organizational organizing, Williams’s contributions intersect with critical psychological and legal examinations of involuntary circumcision. His perspective is preserved within scholarly analyses addressing the emotional and experiential aftermath of the procedure, notably cited in *Objections of a Sentimental Character: The Subjective Dimensions of Foreskin Loss*. Furthermore, his relevance to the human rights dialogue extends to modern legal and human rights assessments, such as *Thinking about infant male circumcision after the Cologne court decision*. Across decades of archival literature, Williams remains recognized as a steadfast champion who helped articulate the subjective, ethical, and legal imperatives central to intactivism.', 'An advocate and legal commentator known for his contributions to the ethical arguments surrounding children''s bodily autonomy.', 'champion', 0, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
