INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-ff88d1ad', 'person', 'Michel Garenne', '**Michel Garenne** is an epidemiologist and demographer whose rigorous scholarship has established him as a key champion of scientific inquiry and human rights within the movement for genital autonomy. His academic work is central to critical discourse surrounding institutional mass circumcision campaigns, providing comprehensive demographic and epidemiological counter-analyses to international public health initiatives in sub-Saharan Africa. Through his critical scrutiny of empirical data, Garenne has consistently challenged the methodological and evidentiary foundations used to justify non-therapeutic genital modifications.

Garenne’s contributions within the archive are anchored by his incisive evaluations of institutional policies, most notably in works such as *Male Circumcision and HIV Prevention in Southern Africa: Questioning WHO Recommendations* and its French-language counterpart, *Circoncision et prévention du VIH en Afrique australe : les recommandations de l''OMS en question*. His analytical rigor is further demonstrated in extensive demographic research, including evaluations of Population-based HIV Impact Assessment (PHIA) surveys that examine age-incidence and prevalence of HIV among intact and circumcised populations. By testing whether real-world observational data support the prophylactic claims of mass intervention trials, Garenne’s research serves as an essential empirical resource for advocates defending the right to bodily integrity.

Beyond quantitative critique, Garenne has engaged in the historical and socio-political interrogation of medical norms. In reflective scholarship comparing 19th-century attitudes toward syphilis with modern HIV/AIDS interventions, he has addressed the recurring institutional tendency to blame natural human anatomy for the transmission of micro-organisms. Furthermore, his involvement in critical appraisals of international technical consultations has helped deconstruct the social, professional, and political networks that drive technical consensus. Through this multifaceted body of work, Garenne remains an essential intellectual authority ensuring that human rights, anatomical normalcy, and scientific integrity are upheld in global public health discourse.', 'French demographer and epidemiologist known for his scientific critiques of male circumcision campaigns in HIV prevention policies.', 'champion', 0, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
