INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-59410e16', 'organization', 'Northwestern University Feinberg School of Medicine', 'The Northwestern University Feinberg School of Medicine, the medical school of Northwestern University located in Chicago, Illinois, is a prominent research institution whose affiliated clinicians and researchers have contributed notable scholarship to the medical, ethical, and anatomical literature surrounding genital autonomy and bodily integrity. Within the broader discourse of human rights and intactivism, work associated with the institution addresses fundamental empirical and systemic questions regarding non-therapeutic neonatal male circumcision as well as pediatric intersex medical interventions.

Scholarly inquiries associated with Feinberg span several core areas vital to the understanding of non-consensual genital modifications. In pediatric education and clinical practice, researchers have evaluated the informational deficits among medical trainees, documenting significant variability in the advice pediatric residents provide to parents concerning the proper hygiene and care of the natural, uncircumcised penis. Institutional contributors have also explored the structural and socioeconomic determinants of the procedure, examining physician availability of neonatal circumcision across the United States alongside the measurable impact that state-level public insurance financing exerts on neonatal circumcision rates. 

Beyond clinical education and healthcare policy, scholarship connected to the institution has advanced discussions in neuroanatomy and bioethics. Research assessing anatomical maps of erogenous sensation has provided empirical data on the functional and sensory differences between circumcised and uncircumcised individuals. Additionally, contributors from Feinberg have engaged with the human rights implications of medically unnecessary pediatric procedures, examining the intersection of conscientious objection, perioperative justice, and the ongoing ethical debates surrounding interventions on children born with intersex traits.', 'A prominent American medical school whose affiliated researchers contribute to clinical literature and bioethical discourse surrounding pediatric health and circumcision.', 'notable', 0, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
