INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-97168d28', 'person', 'Leo Sorger', '**Leo Sorger, M.D.**, stands as an early medical voice and dedicated champion within the human rights movement for genital autonomy. A physician who critically challenged the prevailing medicalization and cultural acceptance of non-therapeutic neonatal circumcision, Sorger provided essential professional credibility to the intactivist cause. His perspectives and clinical critiques have been documented in key educational and historical surveys, including *A Short History of Circumcision in North America: In the Physicians'' Own Words*, which sought to deconstruct routine infant circumcision through the direct testimony of medical practitioners.

Sorger’s contributions extended deeply into institutional advocacy, educational outreach, and organizational leadership. He played an active governance role within the Circumcision Resource Center (CRC), marked by his appointment to the organization''s board and his involvement in strategic correspondence shaping its early publications and public initiatives. Beyond policy and clinical ethics, Sorger’s work engaged with the broader physical and psychological aftermath of infant circumcision; his insights contributed to discourse surrounding foreskin restoration in works such as *Undoing the Doctor''s Deed: Foreskin Restoration*, as well as examinations of societal complacency in writings like *Sowing The Seeds: Bashing Cultural Denial*. Through these concerted efforts, Sorger helped lay vital groundwork for viewing bodily integrity not merely as a medical concern, but as an undeniable ethical imperative.', 'American obstetrician-gynecologist and medical advocate against routine infant circumcision.', 'champion', 0, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
