INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('entity-39fbfec9', 'person', 'Ron Fisher', 'Ron Fisher is an advocate and champion within the genital autonomy and intactivism movement, focusing extensively on the physical, emotional, and psychological recovery of men affected by involuntary neonatal circumcision. His work has contributed substantially to the early development of educational resources, support structures, and peer-counseling networks aimed at validating circumcision-related trauma and promoting the practice of foreskin restoration.

A pivotal figure in peer-led restorative initiatives, Fisher is closely associated with PErSONA Counseling Services, an outreach resource dedicated to offering emotional support, therapeutic guidance, and healing opportunities for men. Extending these efforts into community organizing, he was involved in RECAP (RE-Cover A Penis), a structured support group designed to provide governing policies, practical methods, and collective solidarity for individuals undergoing non-surgical foreskin restoration. 

Through educational advocacy, Fisher has actively challenged medical orthodoxies regarding circumcision and male anatomy. His contributions to the movement''s literature include works such as *Reclaiming Our Bodies: The Physical and Emotional Advantages of Male Foreskin Restoration* and *What the doctor won''t tell you: "Yes, you can be restored!"*, as well as published restoration testimonials. By framing foreskin restoration as both a functional recovery and a profound process of reclaiming one''s body, Fisher has championed the right of individuals to pursue bodily integrity and self-determination.', 'American media producer and activist who leveraged public access television to advance genital autonomy and educational awareness.', 'champion', 0, 3.0, 'C', '', '', '', '', '')
