INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('saving-our-sons', 'organization', 'Saving Our Sons', '### Organizational Overview

**Saving Our Sons** is a grassroots maternal advocacy organization established to provide emotional support, peer guidance, and clinical resources to mothers, fathers, and expecting parents navigating the decision to leave their infant sons intact.

### Countering Generational Coercion

In American culture, parental decisions regarding circumcision are frequently derailed by intense familial pressure—particularly from grandparents, partners, or peer groups reciting the ''look like his father'' trope. Saving Our Sons was founded specifically to address this psychological and social pressure cooker. The network provides expecting mothers with evidence-based counter-arguments, emotional solidarity, and practical tools to maintain their boundary against hospital and familial coercion.

### Educational Outreach

The organization produces high-impact hospital materials, including brightly colored bassinet warning cards reading *''STOP: Do Not Circumcise - Keep Me Intact''*, protecting newborns from accidental surgery during nursery shifts. Through vibrant social media campaigns and local community chapters, Saving Our Sons has saved tens of thousands of infant boys from unnecessary surgical trauma.', 'Grassroots parental movement empowering mothers and families across North America to resist cultural and clinical pressure and keep their sons intact.', 'Grassroots Maternal & Parental Advocacy Network', 0, 4.8, 'A', 'A grassroots maternal bulwark challenging the generational inertia of hospital circumcision through solidarity and education.', '2012–Present', 'Your Whole Baby, Intact America, Bloodstained Men', 'Maternal advocacy, peer counseling, countering generational pressure, family conflict de-escalation', 'Over 100,000 families supported through peer counseling; Nationwide distribution of ''Do Not Circumcise'' hospital bassinet placards.')
