INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('glen-callender', 'person', 'Glen Callender', '### Biography

Glen Callender is an acclaimed Canadian writer, activist, and public educator whose creative campaigns have transformed the landscape of child genital autonomy in Canada and beyond. In 2010, motivated by his own discovery of the anatomical losses caused by infant circumcision, Callender founded the **Canadian Foreskin Awareness Project (CAN-FAP)**.

### Innovative Activism

Recognizing that traditional medical debates often failed to penetrate the general public, Callender pioneered sex-positive, humorous, and culturally engaging tactics. He launched the annual **Foreskin Pride Day** in Vancouver, drawing global media coverage from major outlets including CBC, CTV, *The Globe and Mail*, and international press. 

Callender’s writings articulate the profound aesthetic and sensual richness of the intact body, rejecting the puritanical framework that treats the foreskin as a disease vector. His work has educated hundreds of thousands of Canadians and served as a blueprint for grassroots intactivist media strategy worldwide.', 'Visionary Canadian activist and founder of the Canadian Foreskin Awareness Project (CAN-FAP) and Foreskin Pride rallies.', 'Author / Activist / Founder of CAN-FAP', 0, 4.8, 'A', 'A charismatic pioneer who revitalized Canadian intactivism through body positivity, unapologetic humor, and media savvy.', '2000s–Present', 'Canadian Foreskin Awareness Project (CAN-FAP), Foreskin Pride, Vancouver Human Rights Community', 'Genital autonomy, sex-positive education, grassroots protest design, media relations', 'Founded CAN-FAP in 2010; Launched international ''Foreskin Pride'' phenomenon; Keynote speaker at genital autonomy symposia worldwide.')
