INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('edgar-j-spratling', 'person', 'Edgar J. Spratling, M.D.', '### Historical Role

Dr. Edgar J. Spratling was an American physician and alienist who served on the medical staff of the Matteawan State Hospital for the Criminally Insane in New York during the late 19th century. Spratling is historically significant as an exemplar of the Victorian medical crusade that transformed circumcision from an ancient religious rite into an aggressive pseudo-scientific psychiatric therapy.

### The Anti-Masturbation Mania

In his 1895 paper, *''Masturbation in the Adult''*, published in the *Medical Record*, Dr. Spratling argued that the intact prepuce was an inherently dangerous anatomical defect that provoked chronic reflex neurosis, leading patients into masturbatory addiction, moral decay, and violent criminality. Spratling advocated for involuntary circumcision of asylum inmates, claiming that excising the sensitive mucosal tissue would reduce sensual temptation and restore mental discipline.

### Legacy in Manufacturing ''Normal''

Spratling''s writings, along with those of Dr. Lewis Sayre and Dr. John Harvey Kellogg, laid the institutional groundwork for American circumcision exceptionalism. By wrapping moral panic in the guise of surgical hygiene, Spratling and his contemporaries convinced generation of American doctors that the natural male body was inherently pathological—a dangerous fallacy that took more than a century to begin dismantling.', 'Victorian-era asylum physician at Matteawan State Hospital who authored 1895 papers promoting circumcision to curb masturbation and moral insanity.', 'Victorian Alienist / Historical Proponent', 0, 0.5, 'F', 'A quintessential architect of Victorian medicalized anti-sex hysteria whose pseudoscience helped launder ritual cutting into American hospital routines.', '1890s–1910s', 'Matteawan State Hospital for the Criminally Insane, New York State Medical Society', 'Victorian reflex neurosis, anti-masturbation therapies, involuntary asylum surgery', 'Published 1895 treatise ''Masturbation in the Adult'' in Medical Record; Coined bizarre claims linking intact preputial mucosa to insanity and epilepsy.')
ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET
  name=excluded.name,
  description=excluded.description,
  tagline=excluded.tagline,
