INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('max-malejian', 'person', 'Max Malejian, M.D.', '### Clinical Profile

Dr. Max Malejian is an American pediatric surgeon who gained national prominence within surgical and legal circles for his candid clinical documentation of catastrophic injuries caused by routine neonatal circumcision. While hospital billing departments routinely claimed complication rates below 0.2%, Malejian''s clinical registry exposed a continuous stream of traumatic emergencies caused by high-speed, unvisualized clamping devices.

### Exposing Clamp Failure

In multiple expert consultations and clinical conferences, Dr. Malejian detailed the devastating mechanics of neonatal circumcision tools, specifically the Mogen clamp and Plastibell ring. He documented cases of partial and total glans amputation, severe denudation of penile shaft skin, and catastrophic hemorrhages requiring emergency blood transfusions.

Malejian forcefully rejected the medical establishment''s minimization of these tragedies, arguing that performing blind amputations on moving, unanesthetized newborns inevitably creates an unacceptable margin of surgical error. His whistleblowing has provided crucial evidence for product liability litigation against device manufacturers and informed legal challenges against non-consensual neonatal surgery.', 'Pediatric surgeon who courageously documented and condemned catastrophic neonatal circumcision complications, lacerations, and surgical amputations.', 'Pediatric Surgeon / Whistleblower', 0, 4.6, 'A', 'A clinical truth-teller exposing the high frequency of traumatic surgical emergencies concealed beneath hospital PR and underreporting.', '1990s–Present', 'American College of Surgeons, Pediatric Trauma Registry', 'Pediatric reconstructive surgery, surgical clamp defects, emergency glans reattachment, hospital complication auditing', 'Expert testimony in landmark clamp product liability cases; Published clinical warnings regarding Mogen and Plastibell clamp slippage.')
ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET
  name=excluded.name,
  description=excluded.description,
  tagline=excluded.tagline,
