INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('boyd-winslow', 'person', 'Boyd H. Winslow, M.D.', '### Professional Background

Dr. Boyd H. Winslow, M.D., is an American pediatric urologist who practiced for decades at Children''s Hospital of The King''s Daughters in Norfolk, Virginia. Throughout his career, Dr. Winslow was one of the most prolific pediatric surgeons in the Mid-Atlantic region, performing thousands of circumcisions as well as complex reconstructive repairs for children suffering from congenital anomalies and circumcision complications.

### Candid Reflections in ''American Circumcision''

Dr. Winslow gained widespread attention outside the surgical community through his extensive on-camera interview in Brendon Marotta''s documentary *American Circumcision* (2017). In the film, Winslow spoke with striking, rare candor about his surgical career, acknowledging that he had personally circumcised thousands of boys and performed countless reconstructive revisions for meatal stenosis, skin bridges, and scarred tissue.

While defending the procedure as a cultural reality and emphasizing his clinical care, Winslow admitted the profound moral and ethical questions raised by intactivists, confessing that if a society were designing medicine from scratch on pure evidence, routine infant circumcision would never be instituted. His testimony offered viewers an unvarnished window into the mindset of mainstream American pediatric surgery.', 'Renowned pediatric urologist who acknowledged performing thousands of circumcisions before speaking candidly about surgical harms and complication scale in ''American Circumcision''.', 'Pediatric Urologist', 0, 3.2, 'C', 'A complex clinical figure representing the surgical establishment grappling with the cognitive dissonance of generational practice.', '1970s–2020s', 'Children''s Hospital of The King''s Daughters, Eastern Virginia Medical School, American Urological Association', 'Pediatric urology, hypospadias repair, post-circumcision revisions, meatal stenosis', 'Featured interview in Brendon Marotta''s 2017 documentary ''American Circumcision''; Performed over 10,000 surgeries; Authored surgical textbooks on pediatric urological repair.')
