INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('jutta-reisinger', 'person', 'Jutta Reisinger, M.D.', '### Clinical Whistleblowing

Dr. Jutta Reisinger (frequently cited as Dr. Yut Risinger in early intactivist transcripts) is an Austrian physician and neonatal health specialist who became a prominent European critic of routine circumcision after witnessing American neonatal surgical routines during an international clinical fellowship.

### Documenting Infant Agony

Coming from a European medical tradition where routine infant circumcision is virtually non-existent and viewed as an ethical aberration, Dr. Reisinger was horrified by the assembly-line procedures she observed in American nurseries. She documented that despite token applications of topical cream, infants subjected to mechanical restraint on ''circumstraint'' boards suffered profound physiological shock, evidenced by:
- Heart rates soaring beyond 200 beats per minute;
- Violent apnea and breath-holding spells;
- Palpable tremors and prolonged neuroendocrine cortisol spikes lasting for days post-surgery.

### The ''Elephant in the Hospital''

Dr. Reisinger''s eyewitness accounts were featured prominently in European media and in the 2021 documentary *Child Circumcision: An Elephant in the Hospital*. Her observations challenged the cognitive defense mechanisms of American healthcare workers who normalize infant screams as ''just fussiness'', reminding the international medical community that newborns possess acute pain sensitivity without the psychological capacity to understand or process surgical mutilation.', 'Austrian physician whose published clinical eyewitness testimonies documented the severe neuro-hormonal shock and trauma infants suffer during hospital circumcision.', 'Physician / Neonatal Pain Specialist', 0, 4.8, 'A', 'An Austrian clinical observer whose compassionate testimony broke through medical desensitization to reveal raw infant agony.', '1990s–Present', 'Austrian Pediatric Society, European Bioethics Forum', 'Neonatal nociception, surgical trauma, neuroendocrine stress markers, medical student desensitization', 'Authored widely cited clinical observations on neonatal agony during Plastibell and Gomco clamping; Featured in European documentary ''Child Circumcision: An Elephant in the Hospital''.')
