INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('dayo-kim', 'person', 'Dayo Kim, Ph.D.', '### The South Korean Research Context

Dr. Dayo Kim is a South Korean medical researcher and biostatistician who co-authored one of the most widely cited comparative studies on adult male sexual function in modern urological history. Unlike Western nations where circumcision status is heavily stratified by generation, South Korea experienced a rapid post-WWII American military introduction of circumcision, creating a unique cohort where circumcised and intact men lived side-by-side in identical cultural and socio-economic conditions.

### The 2007 BJU International Study

In 2007, Dr. Kim and Dr. Myung-Geun Pang published *''Sexual function and satisfaction in circumcised and intact men''* in the *British Journal of Urology International* (Vol. 99, Issue 5). The study surveyed over 250 adult men across extensive validated sexual health domains.

The findings were unequivocal:
- Circumcised men reported significantly decreased masturbatory pleasure compared to intact men ($p < 0.05$);
- Circumcised men experienced higher rates of delayed orgasm and required markedly greater friction and force to reach climax;
- Men circumcised later in adult life overwhelmingly reported that their sexual enjoyment was superior prior to surgery.

Dr. Kim''s research dealt a devastating blow to the claim that circumcision has no adverse effect on adult sexual functioning.', 'Co-author of the landmark 2007 BJU International study in South Korea documenting significant sexual function and pleasure deficits in circumcised men.', 'Biostatistical Researcher / Andrologist', 0, 4.7, 'A', 'Pioneered cross-cohort sexual function research in East Asia, proving that adult sexual satisfaction directly declines following preputial excision.', '2000s–Present', 'Eulji University School of Medicine, BJU International, Korean Andrology Association', 'Sexual function surveys, masturbatory satisfaction, penile sensitivity thresholds, South Korean circumcision epidemiology', '2007 Publication of ''Sexual function and satisfaction in circumcised and intact men'' in BJU International with Dr. Myung-Geun Pang.')
