INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('myung-geun-pang', 'person', 'Myung-Geun Pang, Ph.D.', '### Academic Career

Dr. Myung-Geun Pang is an internationally renowned South Korean professor of andrology and reproductive biology at Chung-Ang University. With extensive expertise in male reproductive physiology and cellular biology, Dr. Pang collaborated with Dr. Dayo Kim on the landmark 2007 study examining adult sexual outcomes following circumcision.

### Scientific Importance

Pang’s work helped shift the global medical debate from abstract moral assertions to verifiable neuro-sensory mechanics. His research explained *why* circumcised men experienced decreased sexual satisfaction: the removal of thousands of specialized mechanoreceptors, fine-touch Meissner’s corpuscles, and the mobile glide sleeve permanently impairs the natural tactile feedback loop of the male orgasm. Dr. Pang’s scholarship remains a foundational reference cited throughout genital autonomy legal and scientific briefs worldwide.', 'Renowned South Korean andrologist whose 2007 BJU International research proved the essential role of preputial nerve tissue in male sexual pleasure.', 'Professor of Andrology & Reproductive Biology', 0, 4.7, 'A', 'A distinguished professor of reproductive medicine whose clinical findings shattered the myth of foreskin redundancy.', '1990s–Present', 'Chung-Ang University Department of Animal Biotechnology, Eulji University, Korean Society for Reproductive Medicine', 'Andrology, reproductive endocrinology, sexual biomechanics, histological nerve density', 'Co-author of Kim & Pang (2007) in BJU International; Recipient of national academic honors in Korean reproductive biology.')
