INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('tristan-huff', 'person', 'Tristan Huff', '### Activism and Legal Advocacy

Tristan Huff is an American civil rights organizer and human rights advocate based in Denver, Colorado. As a regional leader within the intactivist movement, Huff has been at the forefront of translating ethical critiques of infant genital cutting into aggressive judicial strategies.

### The Denver District Court Filings

Huff spearheaded high-profile legal filings in the Denver District Court on behalf of injured children and bodily integrity coalitions. His legal arguments challenged the constitutionality of parental proxy consent for permanent, non-therapeutic genital surgery, asserting that minors possess an inalienable right to equal protection under the 14th Amendment and the Colorado state constitution.

Beyond the courtroom, Huff has organized street protests, public debates, and educational seminars across the Mountain West, connecting grassroots activists with national legal teams at Intact Global and GALDEF.', 'Colorado intactivist organizer and civil rights plaintiff who spearheaded landmark legal filings in Denver District Court demanding bodily autonomy for minors.', 'Civil Rights Litigant / Community Organizer', 0, 4.7, 'A', 'A determined community organizer bringing the battle for child bodily integrity directly into state judicial dockets.', '2015–Present', 'Intact Global, Colorado Genital Autonomy Coalition, Denver Intactivist Community', 'Constitutional rights of minors, state district court litigation, street activism, municipal policy reform', 'Filed pioneering civil rights complaints in Denver District Court; Organized Rocky Mountain regional intactivist educational forums.')
