INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('child-circumcision-elephant-in-the-hospital', 'organization', 'Child Circumcision: An Elephant in the Hospital', '### Overview

*Child Circumcision: An Elephant in the Hospital* is a 2021 European documentary film that investigates the deep-seated institutional denial and ethical dissonance surrounding non-therapeutic pediatric circumcision in modern hospitals.

### The ''Elephant'' Metaphor

The film takes its title from the psychological concept of the ''elephant in the room''—a colossal, obvious reality that medical professionals and parents agree not to acknowledge. Through poignant interviews with European physicians (including Austrian pain specialist Dr. Jutta Reisinger), legal scholars, and adult men living with surgical trauma, the film dismantles the polite fiction that circumcision is a minor, inconsequential intervention.

The documentary is particularly praised for contrasting the calm, scholarly European medical consensus (which overwhelmingly regards infant cutting as a human rights violation) with the aggressive commercialization of the surgery in American private healthcare systems.', 'Groundbreaking 2021 European documentary exploring the clinical contradictions, infant trauma, and ethical reckoning within hospital surgical suites.', 'Documentary Film', 0, 4.8, 'A', 'A powerful European cinematic lens exposing the systemic psychological denial enabling hospital genital cutting.', '2021–Present', 'European Genital Autonomy Coalition, Dr. Jutta Reisinger, GAIN', 'Clinical ethics, documentary investigation, hospital culture, infant trauma, European medical perspectives', 'Premiered across European human rights film festivals; Featured eyewitness testimony from Austrian physician Dr. Jutta Reisinger and circumcised men.')
