INSERT INTO entities (id, type, name, description, tagline, role, featured, rating_score, rating_grade, rating_quote, years_active, affiliations, core_focus, key_milestones)
VALUES ('intact-global', 'organization', 'Intact Global', '### Legal Mission

**Intact Global** is an American non-profit civil rights and legal defense organization directed by attorney and activist **Eric Clopper**. The organization’s mission is to secure universal legal protection for all children against non-consensual genital cutting through federal and state constitutional litigation.

### The Equal Protection Strategy

Intact Global’s core legal strategy challenges the double standard in American statutory law, which criminalizes all forms of Female Genital Mutilation (FGM) under strict federal and state penal codes while permitting identical or more severe surgical amputations on healthy male newborns. Intact Global argues that this disparity constitutes unconstitutional sex-based discrimination under the Equal Protection Clause of the 14th Amendment.

### Hadachek v. State of Oregon

In March 2025, Intact Global achieved an unprecedented legal milestone by drafting and filing *Hadachek v. State of Oregon* in the U.S. District Court. The lawsuit contends that Oregon’s statutory exemption permitting male circumcision violates the civil rights of male infants and demands injunctive relief prohibiting licensed physicians from performing non-therapeutic cutting on healthy minors. Intact Global represents the cutting edge of the contemporary intactivist movement’s transition from public education to binding judicial precedent.', 'Civil rights legal foundation directed by attorney Eric Clopper, spearheading federal litigation and equal protection lawsuits to end forced genital cutting.', 'Legal Advocacy & Human Rights Non-Profit', 1, 4.9, 'A+', 'A legal powerhouse bringing cutting-edge constitutional litigation to state and federal courts to enforce equal bodily protection for all children.', '2020–Present', 'Eric Clopper, Tristan Huff, GALDEF, Equal Protection Project', 'Constitutional civil rights litigation, 14th Amendment Equal Protection, child protection statutes, state legislative reform', 'Filed the landmark federal civil rights lawsuit Hadachek v. State of Oregon in 2025; Mobilized national legal defense funds for victims of non-therapeutic genital surgery.')
