VALUES ('helen-a-weiss', 'person', 'Helen A. Weiss, Ph.D.', '### Academic Overview

Dr. Helen A. Weiss, Ph.D., is a Professor of Epidemiology and Biostatistics at the London School of Hygiene & Tropical Medicine (LSHTM). Dr. Weiss is one of the world''s most influential biostatisticians in the field of global infectious disease, having authored dozens of seminal papers on HIV prevention in Sub-Saharan Africa.

### The Circumcision HIV Hypothesis

In 2000 and 2008, Dr. Weiss was the lead author on widely cited meta-analyses examining male circumcision and risk of HIV infection in African men. Her statistical synthesis of observational data concluded that circumcised men had a significantly lower risk of acquiring HIV, providing the theoretical and epidemiological foundation that prompted the World Health Organization (WHO) and the President''s Emergency Plan for AIDS Relief (PEPFAR) to fund massive mass-circumcision drives across southern and eastern Africa.

### Methodological Debates

While celebrated within institutional global health bodies, Dr. Weiss''s models have faced intense scrutiny from bioethicists and independent epidemiologists. Critics pointed out that ecological correlations failed to account for profound regional confounders (such as differing sexual networks, viral subtype distributions, and hygiene infrastructure) and that observational associations could not prove surgical causation. Her work remains a focal point in the international debate over whether surgical interventions can substitute for education and barrier protection.', 'Leading statistician at the London School of Hygiene & Tropical Medicine whose meta-analyses were central to WHO/UNAIDS adult circumcision HIV campaigns.', 'Epidemiologist & Biostatistician', 0, 3.0, 'C', 'A prominent global health statistician whose influential meta-analyses provided epidemiological cover for contested VMMC programs in Africa.', '1990s–Present', 'London School of Hygiene & Tropical Medicine (LSHTM), World Health Organization (WHO), UNAIDS', 'Infectious disease epidemiology, clinical trial design, Sub-Saharan HIV modeling, Cochrane reviews', 'Lead author on early 2000s meta-analyses claiming 60% observational association between circumcision and lower HIV rates in Africa; Consultant to WHO VMMC guidelines.')
